   define('ALLOW_REMOTE_ACCESS', true);
   add_filter('rest_pre_dispatch', 'my_allow_cors');
   function my_allow_cors($server) {
       header("Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *");
       return $server;
   }
   ```

   Replace `*` with the specific domain name if you want to restrict access to only that domain.

2. **Use a Proxy:**
   Another solution is to use a proxy server to make requests to the WordPress API from your Next.js application. Create an API route in your Next.js project and write a script that makes a request to the WordPress API using the `fetch()` function. This way, the browser will see the request as coming from your own domain, bypassing the CORS error.

3. **Install CORS Middleware:**
