 I'd be happy to help you write a Google Apps Script that searches for a place name in a given column and stores its latitude and longitude in two other columns. Here's an example of how you could implement this using the Google Maps Geocoding API:

```javascript
function searchPlacesAndLogCoordinates() {
  // Replace 'SheetName' with the actual name of your Google Sheets spreadsheet.
  const sheetName = "SheetName";
  const apiKey = "YOUR_API_KEY"; // Get your Google Maps API key from the Google Cloud Console

  const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  const sheet = ss.getActiveSheet();
  const dataRange = sheet.getDataRange();
  const values = dataRange.getValues();

  for (let i = 0; i < values.length; i++) {
    const placeName = values[i][0]; // Assuming place names are located in column A
    const geocoder = Maps.newGeocoder();

    try {
      const location = geocoder.geocode(placeName)[0].geometry.location;
      sheet.getRange(i + 1, 2).setValue(location.lat); // Store latitude in column B
      sheet.getRange(i + 1, 3).setValue(location.lng); // Store longitude in column C
      Logger.log(`Successfully logged coordinates for ${placeName}`);
    } catch (error) {
      Logger.log(`Failed to log coordinates for ${placeName}: ${error}`);
    }
  }
}

// Run the function
searchPlacesAndLogCoordinates();
```

This script assumes the place names are located in column A, so it logs the latitude and longitude into columns B and C respectively. Make sure to replace `"SheetName"` with the actual name of your Google Sheets spreadsheet and get your Google Maps API key from the Google Cloud Console.

