        document.getElementById('chooseImage').addEventListener('click', function() {
            document.getElementById('imageInput').click();
        });

        document.getElementById('imageInput').addEventListener('change', function(event) {
            var reader = new FileReader();
            reader.onload = function() {
                document.body.style.backgroundImage = 'url(' + this.result + ')';
            };
            reader.readAsDataURL(event.target.files[0]);
        });
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This HTML page includes a "Choose Desktop Background" button that triggers the file input when clicked. When a user selects an image, it reads the selected file as a data URL and sets the background image of the webpage accordingly. Note that this example uses JavaScript to handle the file selection and reading process.

